A||N||4||ccollins||Catalytic Convertor Question||||1||
Z||000000||ccollins||04-02-2001||10:53 AM||||I was in the process of having a mechanic give me an estimate on a exhaust manifold replacement and he mention that there was something missing from my catalytic convertor. <P>There is a little nipple looking thing on the side of it (toward the front of the car) that is not hooked up to anything.  It's kind of half circle looking.  There is some exhaust coming out of it.  <P>Does anyone know what this is? And where/what it might hook up to. <P>(87 GT Stock V6) <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||04-02-2001||11:37 AM||||I believe that's for air injection into the converter.  Someone will correct me if I'm wrong.  I don't know if all converters have it, but that likely means the other end of that tube is also open, somewhere around the engine.<P>Someone with a better idea, let us know.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-02-2001||11:40 AM||||It doesn't sound like the original cat. Some cars had an A.I.R. pump that pumped air into the cat to aid in reducing emissions. I think they stopped doing that around 80/81. (for cars, I think they still did it for trucks)<BR>The Fiero never had the pump.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||04-02-2001||11:42 AM||||That's there in case the engine uses air injection, but since the Fiero doesn't, it's not used. That should have been obvious to the mechanic.<P>You can get cats with or without the port. Your's was replaced with a universal. No big deal.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||gearhead313||04-02-2001||11:48 AM||||yeppers, just plug it up somehow and don't worry about it||||reg||1
